{
  "v": 1,
  "about": "Tin Hat calls round (security review 2026-10-26, M1 + M2): shared test vectors for the pure call rules. Byte-identical copies: desktop crates/app/src/testvectors/calls.json (the owner), web src/features/calls/testvectors/calls.json, mobile core src/testvectors/calls.json. Contract: share claude/tinhat-security-review/fixes/calls-round/DESIGN.md. Sections: focus = focusDecision (which call service a join uses and whether the user must be asked); sfuUrl = the LiveKit address a call service may answer with; recipients = keyRecipients v2 (who may receive our media key); rotation = the rotate-on-leave planner (a timeline of recipient sets in, actions out); intake = the per-device index book-keeping receivers already use (noteIndex). Member shorthand {s,d,c,f,a,sk,patch} expands to the msc3401 session membership Tin Hat writes (see memberTemplate); patch merges into content (objects merge, arrays and scalars replace, null removes the key). Every case field not given comes from defaults. In joined, a user mapped to null is a member the client does not know yet (lazy-loaded member list: membershipOf returns nothing) and must be treated as not joined, never defaulted to join; users absent from joined are joined. In devices, a user mapped to a list is a known device list (an empty list = no devices left); absent = unknown, which excludes no one. A rotation step may carry note {to, keys}: Planner.noteHolders(to, keys) runs right before that step (a key sent outside the planner: join / ladder / steady / refresh announces; those devices hold it from then on). Ids in recipients/rotation are 'user|device', sorted by byte order.",
